%p
  A client will be available for matching if they meet the requirements in the
  %strong Method used to determine which clients to sync with CAS
  as set on the Site Config page in the associated HMIS Warehouse, or if they are a non-HMIS client and have been marked available.
.c-tag.c-tag--full-width{class: "c-tag--#{@client.is_available_for_matching? ? 'success' : 'warning'}"}
  .c-tag__wrapper
    .c-tag__icon.c-tag__icon--sm
      .icon-checkmark
    .c-tag__content
      %span.c-tag__label=@client.available_text
      - if can_reject_matches?
        .c-tag__action
          = render 'park_client_form'
%hr
- if @client.unavailable_as_candidate_fors.exists?
  %p
    In addition to the overall availability status, which prevents matching on any route, clients may be blocked from matching vacancies on specific routes.  Below is a list of routes for which this client is blocked.  Blocking can occur due to active matches, successful matches, or manual "parking."
  %p
    Configuration each route will determine if a client is blocked from one or more routes when actively involved in a match or successful in a match.
  .blocked-on-routes
    %p.m-2.mt-4.muted-text
      - if @client.unavailable_fors_include_active_match?
        %em This client is actively in a match and will be blocked from matching as noted below:
      - else
        - if UnavailableAsCandidateFor.expiration_length.positive?
          %em This client was successful in a match and has been blocked from matching on the same route for #{UnavailableAsCandidateFor.describe_expiration_length}.
        - else
          %em Clients are blocked from matching on the same route after a complete and successful match.
    %p.m-2.mt-4.muted-text
      %em #{@client.name} will not match any vacancies on the following routes:
    %ul.ml-2.c-detailed-list<
      - @client.unavailable_as_candidate_fors.sort_by(&:created_at).reverse.each do |uf|
        - next unless uf.route.active?
        %li
          .c-detailed-list__item.mb-4
            %span.c-detailed-list__label
              = uf.route&.title || ''
              %br
              - if uf.reason == UnavailableAsCandidateFor::ACTIVE_MATCH_TEXT
                - if uf.match.present?
                  %em Active match
                  (started: #{uf.match.created_at.to_date})
                - else
                  %em Active match
              - else
                - details = []
                - details << "created: #{uf.created_at.to_date}" if uf.created_at.present?
                - details << "expires: #{uf.expires_at.to_date}" if uf.expires_at.present?
                - if uf.reason.present?
                  %em= uf.reason
                  - if details.any?
                    (#{details.join(', ')})
            - if Client.editable_by(current_user).where(id: @client.id).exists?
              %span.c-detailed-list__value= link_to 'Make Available', client_unavailable_on_route_path(@client, uf), method: :delete, class: 'btn btn-sm btn-secondary', data: { confirm: "Are you sure you would like #{@client.name} to be available for matching on the #{uf.route&.title}?" }
